hooks\crypto.test.ts:
(pass) x25519 matches RFC 7748 6.1 [39.87ms]
(pass) argon2id matches RFC 9106 5.3 [42.38ms]
(pass) scrypt matches RFC 7914 12 [111.77ms]
(pass) base64url round-trips every length and refuses anything not strict [8.12ms]
(pass) seal/open round-trips text and 4 KB of bytes, and each seal is different [34.60ms]
(pass) a sealed message that was altered, cut, or sealed to another key is refused, never garbage [23.31ms]
(pass) bundle round-trips at the default cost, and unlock finishes in under 6 s [10999.18ms]
(pass) the header carries m, t, p and a fresh salt, readable without the passphrase [1697.30ms]
(pass) a wrong passphrase fails cleanly [209.72ms]
(pass) a tampered bundle is refused: damaged in copying, altered on purpose, or asking for too much work [255.58ms]
(pass) a bundle of an unknown version, or not a bundle at all, says so [55.66ms]
(pass) a bundle pasted with line breaks and spaces unlocks, and the passphrase is Unicode-normalised [66.26ms]
(pass) the async pair round-trips, and gives byte-identical bundles to the sync pair for the same salt [3843.80ms]
(pass) without setTimeout the async pair falls back to the sync path, with the same output [91.43ms]
(pass) the async pair fails with the same faults as the sync pair [209.28ms]
(pass) passphrase strength scores and explains, and only warns [1.83ms]

